---
/**
 * Privacy policy — version 0.9 of 19/09/2026.
 *
 * Both stores require a policy URL on the listing, and Apple additionally requires
 * (rule 5.1.1(i)) that it be reachable from inside the app: hence the footer link on every
 * page of the site, and the two links placed in the app.
 *
 * The [bracketed] fields — registered address, RNA number, last-updated date — stay as
 * they are until the association is registered. They will be filled in a later commit;
 * nothing here is to be invented.
 *
 * The French text (`politique-de-confidentialite.astro`) is this page's twin: any change
 * of substance happens in both on the same day. There is no Arabic version — a legal text
 * is not machine-translated — and the Arabic footer leads to the French page.
 *
 * Two figures on this page are promises, not settings: the 14-day backup retention (§7 and
 * §6) and the 30-day bin. Changing them elsewhere means changing this page the same day.
 *
 * No `noindex`: unlike the `app/` pages, this one must be findable.
 */
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { routes } from "../../i18n/ui";

const links = routes.en;
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What the Bitaqat Hifd Qor'an app collects, why, for how long, and how to exercise your rights."
  lang="en"
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-600">App</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
      Privacy policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-night-300">
      <strong>Bitaqat Hifd Qor'an mobile app</strong>
      (Android: <span class="font-mono text-sm">com.bitaqat.hifdquran</span> — iOS)<br />
      Last updated: [day month 2026]
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-night-300">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">In short</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The app helps a learner memorise the Qur'an, card by card, under the eyes of a mentor and
          a guardian. It is <strong>free, with no ads, no in-app purchases and no trackers</strong>.
          It asks for <strong>neither the microphone, nor the camera, nor your location</strong>. A
          child exists in it under a <strong>travel name</strong> (a pseudonym) — no real name, no
          email address, no date of birth. Data is
          <strong>hosted in the European Union</strong>. Everything can be deleted from within the
          app, by yourself.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">1. Who is responsible</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The data controller is <strong>Association Bitaqat</strong>, a non-profit association
          under the French law of 1 July 1901, [registered address], [postcode] [town], RNA no.
          [W…], publisher of the app on the app stores.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          For any question or request about your data:
          <strong
            ><a href="mailto:stores@bitaqat-hifd-quran.com" class="underline hover:text-gold-600"
              >stores@bitaqat-hifd-quran.com</a
            ></strong
          >.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
          2. Three roles, and what each one shares
        </h2>

        <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
          The adult account — mentor or guardian
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-2">Only adults have an account with contact details. We keep:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 ps-6">
          <li>
            your <strong>email address</strong> and your <strong>password</strong> (hashed, never
            readable by us);
          </li>
          <li>
            a <strong>display name</strong> you choose — the only thing shown to other users (never
            your email);
          </li>
          <li>
            your <strong>language</strong> and your <strong>notification preferences</strong> (eight
            categories);
          </li>
          <li>
            the <strong>push token</strong> of each device on which you accepted notifications.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          If you choose <strong>"Sign in with Google"</strong> or
          <strong>"Sign in with Apple"</strong>, we receive from that service a technical identifier
          and the email address linked to your account (Apple may offer you a relay address that
          hides yours). We receive nothing else and write nothing to your Google or Apple account.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">The learner profile</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">
          A learner has <strong>no account</strong>: their device connects through an anonymous
          session, with no email address. Their profile holds:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 ps-6">
          <li>
            a <strong>travel name</strong> (pseudonym) and an <strong>avatar</strong> chosen in the
            app;
          </li>
          <li>a <strong>minor or adult</strong> declaration (yes/no, no date of birth);</li>
          <li>
            the <strong>placement profile</strong> from the starting questionnaire (what they can
            already recite);
          </li>
          <li>
            their <strong>progress</strong>: cards, boxes, validation requests, assessments
            received, due dates, badges, rewards, revision programme;
          </li>
          <li>
            their <strong>sessions</strong>: one date per day of actual use,
            <strong>never a duration</strong>;
          </li>
          <li>their in-app <strong>inbox</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          A learner <strong>never types free text</strong>: their requests use predefined messages.
          Free text written by adults (recommendations, rewards) is visible only to the learner
          concerned, their mentor and their guardians.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">What the app does not collect</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">
          No child's real name, no date of birth, no phone number, no postal address, no location,
          no contacts, no photo, no audio or video recording, no advertising identifier, no usage
          duration. No microphone or camera permission is requested from the system — this can be
          checked in the app manifests.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">3. Why, and on what legal basis</h2>
        <!-- Three tables on this page. On a phone they scroll sideways rather than fold: a
             legal basis separated from its purpose no longer means anything. -->
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[36rem] border-collapse text-start">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-200 dark:border-night-700">
                <th scope="col" class="py-2 pe-4 text-start font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
                  Purpose
                </th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-2 pe-4 text-start font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
                  Data
                </th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-2 text-start font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
                  Legal basis (GDPR)
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">
                  Create and run your account, sign you in, send confirmation and
                  forgotten-password emails
                </td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">adult account</td>
                <td class="py-3">performance of a contract (art. 6.1.b)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">
                  Track a learner's progress and let the mentor validate it
                </td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">learner profile</td>
                <td class="py-3">
                  for a minor: consent of the holder of parental responsibility, given twice —
                  through the invitation code, then through the guardian's approval of the pairing;
                  for an adult learner: performance of a contract
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Tell you what needs your attention (notifications)</td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">push tokens, preferences</td>
                <td class="py-3">
                  consent (system permission, revocable), can be switched off per category
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">
                  Protect accounts and children: limit code attempts, log pairings, revocations,
                  manual unlocks and deletions
                </td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">technical identifiers, dates, role of the person acting</td>
                <td class="py-3">legitimate interest (security, art. 6.1.f)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="align-top">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Handle a deletion request made through the website</td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">email address and content of the request</td>
                <td class="py-3">legal obligation (art. 17)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We make <strong>no automated decision</strong> about you, build
          <strong>no profile</strong> for commercial purposes and show
          <strong>no advertising</strong>. Usage measurement is limited to aggregate, anonymous
          counters with no individual profile.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">4. Children</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The app is meant for learners who are often minors, and it is built for that:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 ps-6">
          <li>
            a <strong>guardian</strong> (a parent or a trusted adult chosen by the family, never by
            the mentor) must approve the pairing of a minor with a mentor; without that approval,
            nothing flows between them;
          </li>
          <li>
            the guardian <strong>sees every interaction</strong> and can
            <strong>revoke</strong> the pairing at any time;
          </li>
          <li>only the guardian can <strong>delete a minor's profile</strong>; a mentor never can;</li>
          <li>
            notification content <strong>never shows the travel name</strong> on the lock screen;
          </li>
          <li>on a shared device, only the adult account registers a push token.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          If you believe a profile was created for a minor without a responsible adult's agreement,
          write to us: we will treat it as a priority.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">5. Who sees what</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 ps-6">
          <li><strong>The learner</strong> sees their own journey.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>The paired mentor</strong> sees their learners' progress, requests and
            assessments, and the guardian's display name.
          </li>
          <li><strong>The paired guardian</strong> sees everything about their learner.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>We</strong> (the association and the app's author) access data only to run the
            service, answer a request or fix an incident.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">We do not sell, rent or pass on any data to anyone.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
          6. Where the data lives, and who helps us
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[36rem] border-collapse text-start">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-200 dark:border-night-700">
                <th scope="col" class="py-2 pe-4 text-start font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
                  Provider
                </th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-2 pe-4 text-start font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
                  Role
                </th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-2 text-start font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
                  Location
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4"><strong>Supabase</strong></td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">database, authentication, server functions</td>
                <td class="py-3">European Union (Paris region)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4"><strong>Resend</strong></td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">
                  sending confirmation and forgotten-password emails from
                  <span class="font-mono text-xs">ne-pas-repondre@bitaqat-hifd-quran.com</span>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3">European Union (Ireland region)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4"><strong>Expo</strong> (Expo Application Services)</td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">routing push notifications to Google and Apple</td>
                <td class="py-3">
                  United States — notifications carry no name and no personal text: fixed labels
                  from a catalogue
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">
                  <strong>Google Firebase Cloud Messaging</strong> /
                  <strong>Apple Push Notification service</strong>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">delivering notifications to the device</td>
                <td class="py-3">as per Google and Apple</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4"><strong>Cloudflare</strong></td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">
                  website, email-confirmation and forgotten-password pages, deletion-request form,
                  Turnstile anti-bot check, storage of the encrypted backups (EU region)
                </td>
                <td class="py-3">United States, with points of presence in Europe</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="align-top">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">
                  <strong>Google Play</strong> / <strong>App Store</strong>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">app distribution</td>
                <td class="py-3">as per Google and Apple, under their own policies</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Transfers outside the European Union are covered by the safeguards provided for by the
          GDPR (standard contractual clauses or an adequacy decision) and limited to what is
          strictly necessary — for notifications, a technical token and a catalogue label.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">7. For how long</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[34rem] border-collapse text-start">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-200 dark:border-night-700">
                <th scope="col" class="py-2 pe-4 text-start font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
                  Data
                </th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-2 text-start font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
                  Retention
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Adult account</td>
                <td class="py-3">until you delete it</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Learner profile</td>
                <td class="py-3">
                  until deleted; it then spends <strong>30 days in a bin</strong> from which the
                  guardian can restore it, after which everything is erased
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Anonymous session of a device with no profile</td>
                <td class="py-3"><strong>7 days</strong>, then automatic purge</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Invitation or pairing code</td>
                <td class="py-3"><strong>72 hours</strong>, single use</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Push token</td>
                <td class="py-3">
                  removed after <strong>90 days</strong> without the app being opened on that
                  device, or as soon as Google or Apple reports it invalid
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Log of pairings, revocations and deletions</td>
                <td class="py-3">with the profile concerned</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-ink-100 align-top dark:border-night-800">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Deletion request received through the website</td>
                <td class="py-3">as long as it takes to verify and process it</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="align-top">
                <td class="py-3 pe-4">Backups</td>
                <td class="py-3">
                  an encrypted copy of the database is made every night and kept for
                  <strong>14 days</strong> with a storage provider (Cloudflare, European Union),
                  then destroyed automatically. It is never used to restore a deleted account or
                  profile
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">
          A deleted adult account <strong>does not take its learners with it</strong>: an adult is a
          teacher or a guardian, never an owner. Their profiles go back to "waiting for a teacher",
          and the assessments already given stay in their history, without an author's name.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">8. Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You have the rights of <strong>access</strong>, <strong>rectification</strong>,
          <strong>erasure</strong>, <strong>portability</strong>, <strong>objection</strong> and
          <strong>restriction</strong>. For a minor, they are exercised by the guardian.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 ps-6">
          <li>
            <strong>From the app</strong>: Settings → Delete my account (adult); Settings → Delete
            my profile (adult learner); child's page → Delete this child's profile (guardian), with
            a <strong>signed export</strong> of the journey handed over on the device for
            portability — never sent by email.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Without the app</strong> (uninstalled, lost phone): the
            <a href={links.suppression} class="underline hover:text-gold-600"
              >Delete an account or a profile</a
            > page on the website. Every request is verified and processed by hand, and we reply to
            you before any deletion.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>By email</strong>:
            <a href="mailto:stores@bitaqat-hifd-quran.com" class="underline hover:text-gold-600"
              >stores@bitaqat-hifd-quran.com</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          You may also lodge a complaint with the French data protection authority, the CNIL (<a
            href="https://www.cnil.fr"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline hover:text-gold-600">www.cnil.fr</a
          >), or with the authority of your own country.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">9. Security</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Encryption in transit (TLS) and at rest with our host; hashed passwords; access rules
          enforced by the database itself, row by row, according to role; invitation codes that
          cannot be guessed, single-use, with limited attempts; logging of sensitive actions; no
          secrets inside the installed app. Irreversible actions (deletion, revocation) require the
          adult's password, never the simple adult gate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">10. Notifications</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The app tells you what needs your attention (validation request, verdict, due date,
          reward, pairing). Each category can be switched off in the account settings; switching
          off means "stop ringing" — the information stays readable in the app's inbox. No
          promotional notification, ever.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">11. Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We will update this page if the app or our providers change. The date at the top is the
          reference; a significant change is announced in the app.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">12. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Association Bitaqat — [registered address], [postcode] [town] —
          <a href="mailto:stores@bitaqat-hifd-quran.com" class="underline hover:text-gold-600"
            >stores@bitaqat-hifd-quran.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
